# Files docker doesn't need to send across to the daemon. Keeps the
# build context small (the whole monorepo would otherwise ship every
# build, including node_modules, target/, etc).

# Dependencies
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store

# Build artefacts
**/dist
**/.next
**/.nuxt
**/.svelte-kit
**/.vite
**/target
**/.cargo-cache

# Test / coverage
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/.pytest_cache

# Editor / OS
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Logs
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# Env (real values live in secrets / .env on the VPS, not in builds)
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Misc
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
LICENSE
**/*.md
beads
.beads
.context-os
